      "worked": "Since $5^x>0$, the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{1}{1+5^{-x}}-\\frac12\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{5^x}{1+5^x}-\\frac12\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{5^x-1}{2(1+5^x)}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\left(\\frac{1}{1+5^x}-\\frac12\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence $f$ is odd.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
